Observations:
    Every element in a (stiffness) weak region should have roughly the same max
    stress sign if stress is smooth. We could also force it to if needed.
    Therefore, "abstrace" maybe isn't needed to avoid cancellation.

    There is a "preferred" sign from the perspective of stress optimization
    (flipping pressures isn't allowed). Modal analysis has no such preference,
    so we should try both +/- weightings for the entire weak region.

==> Thoughts:
    Split up weak regions into sign-coherent regions.
    Test both + and - objectives.
